KG42.register("rules-18d34574242280975af9fc61",{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R004","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Social-welfare clearing objective","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"The market operator implements welfare-maximizing clearing by ordering demand bids in decreasing order and supply offers in increasing order to construct the demand and supply curves. Scope: The study's centralized local double-sided auction. The clearing objective is to maximize total bidders' utility minus total producers' costs, subject to aggregate demand equaling aggregate supply. Scope: The social-welfare optimization of the local double-sided auction.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.social_welfare under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.social_welfare","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"The social-welfare optimization of the local double-sided auction. | The study's centralized local double-sided auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g02-e02"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R004-x-d_i","symbol":"d_i","meaning":"Buyer i's bid amount entering the social-welfare objective as the argument of u_i, and entering the aggregate bid-balance constraint.","kind":"operational","domain":"Buyer bid amount; the cited evidence does not state sign, bounds, or units.","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g02-e02"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R004-x-s_j","symbol":"s_j","meaning":"Seller j's offer amount entering the social-welfare objective as the argument of c_j, and entering the aggregate bid-balance constraint.","kind":"operational","domain":"Seller offer amount; the cited evidence does not state sign, bounds, or units.","unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g02-e02"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-n_B","symbol":"n_B","meaning":"Number of buyers in the social-welfare clearing objective.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g02-e02"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-n_S","symbol":"n_S","meaning":"Number of sellers in the social-welfare clearing objective.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g02-e02"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The market operator implements welfare-maximizing clearing by ordering demand bids in decreasing order and supply offers in increasing order to construct the demand and supply curves. Scope: The study's centralized local double-sided auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The clearing objective is to maximize total bidders' utility minus total producers' costs, subject to aggregate demand equaling aggregate supply. Scope: The social-welfare optimization of the local double-sided auction.","expression":"\\max SW = \\sum_{i=1}^{n_B} u_i(d_i) - \\sum_{j=1}^{n_S} c_j(s_j) \\quad \\text{s.t.} \\quad \\sum_{i=1}^{n_B} d_i = \\sum_{j=1}^{n_S} s_j \\quad (1)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R004-x-d_i","v141-c-R004-x-s_j"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R004-theta-n_B","v141-c-R004-theta-n_S"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g02-e02"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"max SW = ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} u_i(d_i) − ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} c_j(s_j)\ns.t. ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} d_i = ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} s_j (1)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e02","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The objective of the market is to maximize social welfare [18]. Mathematically, social welfare SW is formulated by the sum of the bidders’ utility u minus the sum of producers’ costs c (Eq. (1)). The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement.\n\\[ \\max SW = \\sum_{i=1}^{n_B} u_i(d_i) - \\sum_{j=1}^{n_S} c_j(s_j) \\]\n\\[ \\text{s.t.} \\quad \\sum_{i=1}^{n_B} d_i = \\sum_{j=1}^{n_S} s_j \\quad (1) \\]"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-matching","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.social_welfare","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","quote":"To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e02","quote":"The objective of the market is to maximize social welfare [18]. Mathematically, social welfare SW is formulated by the sum of the bidders’ utility u minus the sum of producers’ costs c (Eq. (1))."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e09","quote":"max SW = ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} u_i(d_i) − ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} c_j(s_j)\ns.t. ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} d_i = ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} s_j (1)"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"434c4b2570e763b9de9d22f5499e6482a08ab940cc73ba55681d443dec699e6e","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Constraint v141-c-R004-C002 has an explicit source objective in Eq. (1): maximize social welfare as buyer utility minus producer cost subject to aggregate bid/offer balance. Constraint v141-c-R004-C001 remains procedural because the source describes the operator's decreasing-bid/increasing-offer ordering but gives no explicit mathematical ordering formula in the cited evidence. B evidence remains unreviewed; this formalization only transcribes the supplied source text.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"C001 describes the local operator's ordering of bids and offers for welfare-maximizing clearing; the frozen graph represents this operator-to-clearing-objective relation by E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"C002 is the social-welfare objective itself and is owned by clearing.social_welfare. The operator edge E001 links the coordinating operator to that clearing objective, consistent with the source's statement that the market operator implements welfare-maximizing clearing."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-x-d_i","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"The buyer bid amount d_i is an argument of the welfare objective in C002. The frozen rule represents that objective at clearing.social_welfare and links it to coordination.local_operator through E001; no separate bidding node belongs to this rule's frozen V."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-x-s_j","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"The seller offer amount s_j is an argument of the welfare objective in C002. The frozen rule represents that objective at clearing.social_welfare and links it to coordination.local_operator through E001; no separate supply node belongs to this rule's frozen V."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-n_B","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"The count n_B indexes the buyer summation in the welfare objective and its balance constraint, both owned by clearing.social_welfare under the operator-linked clearing relation E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-n_S","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"The count n_S indexes the seller summation in the welfare objective and its balance constraint, both owned by clearing.social_welfare under the operator-linked clearing relation E001."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
